00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:37.450
There's also a Nun figurine in the daughter's
room and in the basement.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:41.450
It all leads up to this reveal: Valak has
been haunting Lorraine and her family since

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:43.130
at least 1976.

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:46.460
Then later on in the movie, Lorraine mentions
that the vision she had in Amityville was

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:50.820
the same one she had 7 years ago, meaning
that Valak has been around her family since

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:52.320
at least 1969.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.060
"It was the same one I had 7 years ago.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.540
The demon in your painting is real.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:04.700
We have both seen the same inhuman spirit.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.280
It's a warning.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:09.240
If we keep doing this, you're going to die."

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:14.520
Weird stuff starts happening after Ed Warren
wakes up from a dream in which he saw the

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.460
demon, and couldn't get it out of his head.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.800
The name Valak starts appearing everywhere.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.030
First on the wall in the kitchen, then the
daughter's arts and crafts.

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:27.030
A couple nights later letters appear in the
study, where another Nun statue appears.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:30.100
During one of Lorraine's visions, she ends
up writing the name in her bible during a

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.320
state of panic.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:34.630
After the Warrens head out to England to try
to help the Hodgson family, there's scene

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:38.450
where the church choir music originally heard
in Lorraine's vision can be heard coming from

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:42.770
the kitchen of the Hodgson house and the daughter
Janet claims to see a pair of eyes hiding

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:53.210
in the dark.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:56.300
This is most likely her first vision of Valak
in it's Nun form.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:59.840
Valak tells her to destroy the kitchen to
get the public to believe that the whole thing

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:04.920
was a hoax and reduce the possibility of invention
from the church, but the chapel music and

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:08.790
the sounds of knives sharpening tells me that
she really does see the demon hiding in the

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:09.790
dark.

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:13.150
It's not long after that when Ed and Lorraine
realize the spirit of the old man haunting

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:17.560
the house is being controlled by the demon,
and everything after that is quite obvious...

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:19.989
That is... until the end credits.

00:04:19.989 --> 00:04:23.990
The end title sequence is accompanied by a
series of photos, some of which compare the

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:29.400
actors in the movie to their real life counterparts
as you might often see in "based on a true

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:30.870
story" films.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:35.020
The photos are displayed on an old slide projector,
so when switching from photo to photo, there

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:37.610
is a bit of a gap that lasts a fraction of
a second.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:42.500
Sometimes though, instead of seeing the transitioning
projector in between frames, an image is displayed.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:46.440
It's usually a photo of the house, and some
of them contain the old man sitting on the

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:47.440
chair.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:50.580
If you pause at just the right moment or go
frame by frame, one of these photos shows

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:53.340
the demon Valak standing over the old man's
body.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:57.870
I was actually somewhat startled to come across
this, because I had no idea it was there.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:01.930
Another frame spliced in depicts the demon
standing at the end of the hall, as seen earlier

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:03.710
in the movie at the Warren residence.

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:08.020
I don't know why, but the face is blurred
in each of these photos, and nothing else.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:11.830
Here's another shot that is displayed one
frame later, this one could be more of a teaser

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.050
toward The Nun.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:18.850
Aaaand then there's this lovely portrait,
which is the last one before the credits roll

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:22.060
and we move on to Annabelle Creation.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:25.690
And it takes place way before everything else,
meaning that it's closer to the time period

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:26.750
